HST Office: one optional check of the target format before a document is saved (Sheets functions in Excel files).

Cells that use the HST Sheets functions (DOCSO, DOCTIEN, BODAU, TACHHO, TACHTEN) show #NAME? in
Microsoft Excel. Jobs on OnSave/OnSaveAs cannot cancel a save and do not see the format chosen
in the Save As dialog, so the save code now asks the bundled extension's service
org.hst.office.vi.SaveFormatCheck (an XJob: Model, FilterName; returns false to cancel) right
before storing: on Save, and on Save As / Save a Copy after the file and filter options dialogs
(not for PDF or EPUB export). The extension warns and offers "Chuyển thành giá trị khi lưu"
(hst-save-hst-functions-as-values.patch) / "Vẫn lưu" / "Hủy". Without the service, or when it fails, saving works as before. API saves, hidden documents
and headless runs are not affected.

